### Credentials requests (phase 3). Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Run them in order: the state changes carry over. Restart the backend (or use a fresh demo database)
### to start again from the seed. Fixtures: cred-001 ACTIVE student card, cred-015 BLOCKED, cred-024 DEACTIVATED
### with a PENDING enrollment, cred-039 DEACTIVATED with a COMPLETED enrollment, cred-054 ACTIVE stock card.
@host = https://tarjepafi-api-pafi7k2.azurewebsites.net
# @host = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@upc.edu.pe
@adminPassword = Admin123*

### 0. Sign in as administrator (the deployed demo uses another password: ask the backend owner)
# @name signIn
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@token = {{signIn.response.body.$.token}}

### 1. Settings (any signed-in user)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. List the cards, filtered (expect 2 BLOCKED)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/credentials?status=BLOCKED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Search by text (expect cred-001 and its holder)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/credentials?q=U202312966
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Card holders: by exact code (expect 1), by role (expect 4 teachers)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/card-holders?code=u202312966
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/card-holders?role=TEACHER
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. US10: block without a note (expect 400 NOTE_REQUIRED)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/block
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 6. US10: block with a note (expect 200, status BLOCKED)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/block
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Card found damaged" }

### 7. Blocking again (expect 409 ACTION_NOT_ALLOWED)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/block
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "again" }

### 8. US13: reactivate it (expect 200, ACTIVE)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 9. History of cred-001 (expect two entries, newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. US13: a student with a pending enrollment (expect 422 ENROLLMENT_NOT_COMPLETED)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-024/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 11. US13: the holder already has another active card (expect 409 HOLDER_HAS_ACTIVE_CARD)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-009/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 12. US13: re-enrolled student (expect 200, reason REENROLLMENT in the history)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-039/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 13. US11: link the stock card to a holder without an active card (expect 200)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-054/link-holder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holderCode": "U202311918" }

### 14. US11: same holder again (expect 409 ALREADY_LINKED)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-054/link-holder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holderCode": "U202311918" }

### 15. US11: unknown holder (expect 404 HOLDER_NOT_FOUND)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-055/link-holder
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "holderCode": "U000" }

### 16. US14: create an exception, then replace it, list, remove it
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/permissions/sp-a301
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "effect": "DENY" }

###
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/permissions/sp-a301
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "effect": "ALLOW" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/permissions/sp-a301
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. US14: unknown space (expect 404 SPACE_NOT_FOUND)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/cred-001/permissions/nope
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "effect": "ALLOW" }

### 18. US15: preview, then run (expect the active cards of students with PENDING enrollment), then run again (expect none)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/enrollment-verification/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/enrollment-verification
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/credentials/enrollment-verification
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Catalogues (any signed-in user): 15 spaces, 6 classrooms, 6 courses
GET {{host}}/api/v1/spaces
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/spaces?type=CLASSROOM
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/spaces/sp-a301
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/courses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/class-schedules?teacherId=ch-d0001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/enrollments?scheduleId=sch-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 20. A teacher may not read the cards (expect 403)
# @name teacherIn
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "docente@upc.edu.pe", "password": "Docente123*" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/credentials
Authorization: Bearer {{teacherIn.response.body.$.token}}
